{number: 76}
{title: Work, for the Night is Coming}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Work, for the night is coming,
Work thro' the [Bb] morning [F] hours;
Work while the dew is sparkling,
Work 'mid [C7] springing flowers.
[F] Work when the day grows brighter,
Under the [Bb] glowing [F] sun;
Work, for the night is [Bb] coming,
When [F] man's [C7] work is [F] done.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Work for the night is coming,
Work thro' the [Bb] sunny [F] noon;
Fill brightest hours with labor,
Rest comes [C7] sure and soon.
[F] Give every flying minute
Something to [Bb] keep in [F] store;
Work, for the night is [Bb] coming,
When [F] man [C7] works no [F] more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Work for the night is coming,
Under the [Bb] sunset [F] skies;
While their bright tints are glowing,
Work, for [C7] daylight flies.
[F] Work till the last beam fadeth,
Fadeth to [Bb] shine no [F] more;
Work, while the night is [Bb] dark'ning,
When [F] man's [C7] work is [F] o'er.
{end_of_verse}
